round lantern from 9 P.M. till 11 P.M.; one Lark killed. (S.S.E., 6;
O. M. K.) _Selker_ L.V., Larks, Thrushes, and Starlings at midnight;
three Thrushes killed. (4, S.S.E.; O. M.) _Skerries Rock_ L.H.,
Starlings, Chaffinches, and Linnets going N.W. from 8 A.M. to noon.
Two Goldfinches flying about island at 9.30 A.M.; "very rare." (N.W,
5; B. C. V.) _South Bishop_ L.H., companies of Larks passing from 8.30
A.M. until noon. _Helwick_ L.V., a good many Thrushes during the night;
one killed. (W.S.W., 5; Q. M.) _Nash_ (_E._) L.H., Starlings, Larks,
Fieldfares, and Lapwings; a good many passing to N.W. from 7 to 9 A.M.
(N.N.W., 5; C. G.) _Burnham_ L.H., flocks of Lapwings flying S. all day.

N.E., fresh, showery; 8th, about lantern; wind fresh E.; 9th, one in
daytime; on 10th, 11th, 13th, 14th, and 15th, about lantern at night,
four killed striking on 11th, and several killed and fell overboard
on 13th and 14th; wind S.E. to N.E., gloomy at night, except on 14th;
on 12th, two going N.W. in daytime; 15th, some about ship. (See under
Starling.)

_Barrels Rock Light-ship._--November 9th, some going N., 8 to 11 P.M.;
wind fresh N.E., cloudy; 10th, three going N., 8.30 A.M.; one rested on
ship; wind light N.E., clear; 12th, some going N., midnight to 5 A.M.;
wind light E., gloomy; one killed striking. [Leg and wing received.]
